            {
                "entry_id": "97920a60-bc35-308c-87bb-b4bc14f0f5e5",
                "word": "abigaïl",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2a90d344-55f0-4833-ad9b-6d29dbee8949",
                        "entry_id": "97920a60-bc35-308c-87bb-b4bc14f0f5e5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "abigaïls"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bffdb84c-d35b-3881-88d0-526c56c182ce",
                        "entry_id": "97920a60-bc35-308c-87bb-b4bc14f0f5e5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Femme de chambre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "familiar",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5060f616-2761-4308-8990-37b31c9d548a",
                                "sense_id": "bffdb84c-d35b-3881-88d0-526c56c182ce",
                                "text": "On vit paraître une superbe berline, forme anglaise, à quatre chevaux, remarquable surtout par deux très jolies abigaïls, qui étaient juchées sur le siège du cocher..."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "000a479e-193e-46b3-83ba-b14e05075cb5",
                        "source_entry_id": "97920a60-bc35-308c-87bb-b4bc14f0f5e5",
                        "source_sense_id": "bffdb84c-d35b-3881-88d0-526c56c182ce",
                        "target_lang_word": "abigaïl",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "abigaïl",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ac6bba3-ff1d-33fb-8527-cc2a34616eef",
                                        "entry_id": "20e97de6-6043-366c-9252-e92193c2e403",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lady's maid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58f6c12a-bf88-4c13-ab68-169c7b8b5a23",
                                                "sense_id": "7ac6bba3-ff1d-33fb-8527-cc2a34616eef",
                                                "text": "It was therefore concluded that the Abigails should, by turns, relieve each other on one of his lordship’s horses, which was presently equipped with a side-saddle for that purpose."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f298f187-c4e1-4788-b4ff-fa7c1d30f749",
                                                "sense_id": "7ac6bba3-ff1d-33fb-8527-cc2a34616eef",
                                                "text": "In the servants’ hall two coachmen and three gentlemen’s gentlemen stood or sat round the fire; the abigails, I suppose, were upstairs with their mistresses; the new servants, that had been hired from Millcote, were bustling about everywhere."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "175ab953-87d4-4f14-80b9-b3f662c77f6f",
                        "source_entry_id": "97920a60-bc35-308c-87bb-b4bc14f0f5e5",
                        "source_sense_id": "bffdb84c-d35b-3881-88d0-526c56c182ce",
                        "target_lang_word": "lady's maid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lady's maid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80534e82-7225-3d1d-a2de-8dbf6da872d4",
                                        "entry_id": "8f176b96-b36e-3532-9865-ea49ef634094",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female servant employed by an upper-class woman to attend to her personal needs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "533410ed-7b8e-43a2-ba6a-c58cde953577",
                                                "sense_id": "80534e82-7225-3d1d-a2de-8dbf6da872d4",
                                                "text": "A pretty Girl, the Lady’s Maid,\nWho all her Dress in Order Laid,\nBehind her Mistress simp’ring stood,\nAnd rais’d the youthful ’Squires Blood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35b915c2-75bd-4d82-bc5e-950630974cc6",
                                                "sense_id": "80534e82-7225-3d1d-a2de-8dbf6da872d4",
                                                "text": "He stopped, ran his eye over my dress, which, as usual, was quite simple: a black merino cloak, a black beaver bonnet; neither of them half fine enough for a lady’s-maid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7796b2a6-6deb-49d0-950f-ec17fa997280",
                                                "sense_id": "80534e82-7225-3d1d-a2de-8dbf6da872d4",
                                                "text": "[…] the servant, a neat, plain woman, with a French face and a lady’s maid’s manner, ushered him into a diminutive drawing-room and requested the favour of his name."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e603181-6d16-4add-9ad6-d20c89008ba0",
                                                "sense_id": "80534e82-7225-3d1d-a2de-8dbf6da872d4",
                                                "text": "The cat is the offspring of a cat and the dog of a dog, but butlers and lady’s maids do not reproduce their kind. They have other duties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d2696c1-ed13-4720-b18a-170720b92750",
                                                "sense_id": "80534e82-7225-3d1d-a2de-8dbf6da872d4",
                                                "text": "A first class lady’s maid is required to be a hairdresser, a good packer and an expert needlewoman. Her first duty is to keep her lady's clothes in order and to help her dress, and undress."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
